Modified file

  src/main/java/edu/stonybrook/bmi/hatch/CellSensReader.java
    Derived from loci.formats.in.CellSensReader. Changes for hatch:
    - hands out the stored JPEG tiles of an ETS file without decoding them
      (RawTileSource.getRawTile / getRawTileLayout), reading each tile by its
      chunk-table byte count through one open file per ETS file;
    - looks tiles up through a hash map instead of a list search;
    - keeps an explicit core index -> pyramid map, used for both metadata and
      tile reads;
    - reports a missing ETS folder, and series not stored in an ETS file, as
      errors; closes itself when initialization fails;
    - with a non-zero TILE_ORIGIN, copies the stored tile grid as it is and
      widens the image to it, since tiles cannot be shifted without
      re-encoding (see getRawTileLayout).

Bio-Formats (formats-api, formats-bsd, formats-gpl 8.3.0) is otherwise used
unmodified, as a library. HatchTiffReader and HatchSVSReader subclass its
TIFF and SVS readers.
